WEBVTT

00:00:10.292 --> 00:00:14.292
It's him! After all these years,
it's really him!

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.792
You're stuffed, bear.

00:00:21.208 --> 00:00:23.333
- One night, you said. One night!
- I know...

00:00:23.417 --> 00:00:25.708
You promised to take him
to the authorities.

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:28.583
- I never promised.
- Well, you very heavily implied it.

00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:32.750
I'm sorry, but he was telling the truth.
There really is an explorer.

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:36.792
- What are you doing?
- I'm doing my looking-away face.

00:00:36.875 --> 00:00:39.333
- Are you doing the breathing?
- I'm doing the breathing.

00:00:39.417 --> 00:00:42.250
All we need to do is take him
to the Geographers' Guild.

00:00:42.292 --> 00:00:43.750
- Stop!
- The hand's gone up.

00:00:43.875 --> 00:00:46.417
- We've done quite enough for this bear.
- And the voice.

00:00:46.792 --> 00:00:49.667
- I am taking charge!
- You're taking charge?

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:52.208
Yes! Paddington
is a danger to this family.

00:00:52.292 --> 00:00:54.583
Jonathan is quite irresponsible enough

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:57.417
without throwing a wild animal
into the mix.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:00.500
Hey, Paddington.
Have you seen the paper?

00:01:01.542 --> 00:01:02.708
Gosh.

00:01:02.792 --> 00:01:05.667
You've only been in London a day
and you're already famous.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:07.417
Oh.

00:01:07.542 --> 00:01:10.208
I'm sorry if I wasn't very nice before.

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:14.833
It's just it's a new school and I didn't
want everyone to think I was weird.

00:01:14.917 --> 00:01:18.708
Oh, I understand, Judy.
It's not easy being somewhere new.

00:01:19.958 --> 00:01:21.583
No, it isn't.

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:23.833
He put earwax on my toothbrush!

00:01:24.375 --> 00:01:26.958
Things can be very different
from how you imagined.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.542
Don't let him bother you. Dad's always
been boring and annoying.

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:34.042
Oh, I don't know about that.
More to your father than meets the eye.

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:36.917
- Like what?
- When I first met him,

00:01:36.958 --> 00:01:38.917
he was a very different man.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:42.083
♪ Get your motor running

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:43.542
Whoo!

00:01:43.625 --> 00:01:46.750
- ♪ Head out on the highway
-  Wahey!

00:01:46.833 --> 00:01:49.250
- ♪ Looking for adventure
- That's my girl.

00:01:49.833 --> 00:01:52.167
♪ And whatever comes our way

00:01:53.042 --> 00:01:56.750
- Not gonna let this change us, right?
- No way, baby.

00:01:56.833 --> 00:02:00.167
- ♪ Born to be wild
- We're having a baby!

00:02:04.625 --> 00:02:08.458
But becoming a father
does strange things to a man.

00:02:08.583 --> 00:02:12.208
Be careful, there's a baby here. Step
back, there's a baby coming through.

00:02:12.292 --> 00:02:15.708
Could you keep those ﬂowers away,
please? She's too young for pollen.

00:02:15.792 --> 00:02:18.125
- Where's the bike, darling?
- This is our new car.

00:02:18.208 --> 00:02:20.750
What? It's very beige, isn't it?

00:02:20.833 --> 00:02:22.667
It's a calm and neutral colour. Get in.

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:27.292
The point is, your father loves you
very much. Give him a chance.

00:02:27.375 --> 00:02:28.875
He might just surprise you.

00:02:29.792 --> 00:02:31.250
Oh.

00:02:31.333 --> 00:02:33.833
Maybe you and Dad
just need a fresh start.

00:02:33.917 --> 00:02:34.958
Hmm.

00:02:35.042 --> 00:02:37.708
I suppose I didn't make
the best first impression.

00:02:37.833 --> 00:02:39.875
Don't take this the wrong way but...

00:02:39.958 --> 00:02:42.958
why don't we try to make you
look a bit more presentable?

00:02:43.542 --> 00:02:46.625
Hang on a minute.
You're not talking about...

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:49.125
..the facilities?

00:02:50.708 --> 00:02:54.125
- Relax, Paddington, it's not that bad.
- It is that bad.

00:02:54.208 --> 00:02:58.708
Doesn't it rain enough in this city
without having showers in the house?

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:15.917
The point is, we are parents now
and we have to protect our children.

00:03:16.042 --> 00:03:17.750
We do.

00:03:17.833 --> 00:03:20.583
- They're screaming.
- That's the sound of laughter.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:25.542
Wind. Hot wind. Two hot winds.

00:03:25.625 --> 00:03:27.333
I don't like it.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:31.208
Well, I hope I don't look weird
after all that.

00:03:32.708 --> 00:03:35.000
- Too much?
- Too much.

00:03:35.042 --> 00:03:37.333
Too much?
Well, get me a brush, will you?

00:03:37.792 --> 00:03:41.250
Ah, there it is.

00:03:42.083 --> 00:03:45.208
- That's my old dufﬂe coat.
- Actually, it was mine first.

00:03:45.333 --> 00:03:47.458
Well, long before that, it was mine.

00:03:47.583 --> 00:03:49.708
- Oh, was it, Mr Brown?
- Really?

00:03:49.792 --> 00:03:53.167
- He wore it on his first day at school.
- It's lovely.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:55.875
Wooden buttons for ease of paw.

00:03:55.917 --> 00:03:58.792
And these two sandwich compartments
are an excellent idea.

00:03:58.875 --> 00:04:01.042
I must say, it suits you very well.

00:04:01.125 --> 00:04:03.625
I never thought
I'd like a human coat, but...

00:04:03.708 --> 00:04:05.250
You look like one of the family.

00:04:06.875 --> 00:04:09.750
You're not going to send Paddington
to the authorities, are you?

00:04:11.708 --> 00:04:13.625
You will try the Geographers' Guild?

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:22.667
Yes, alright, we'll see
if they know anything.

00:04:22.833 --> 00:04:25.542
- But if it's a dead end...
- I'm sure it won't be.

00:04:25.667 --> 00:04:27.458
Thank you very much, Mr Brown.

00:04:34.958 --> 00:04:38.167
You must get a lot of strange customers
in here.

00:04:38.417 --> 00:04:40.250
You don't know the half of it, love.

00:04:40.375 --> 00:04:44.083
I've had bishops, magicians, bears,
contortionists.

00:04:44.167 --> 00:04:45.792
Did you say bears?

00:04:45.833 --> 00:04:47.958
Yeah. Had one in here last night,
actually.

00:04:48.042 --> 00:04:51.583
Oh! How fascinating. I don't suppose
you remember where you took him?

00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:54.292
- 'Fraid I can't tell you that, love.
- Why not?

00:04:54.375 --> 00:04:57.583
- It's against the Cabbie's Code, innit?
- The what?

00:04:57.667 --> 00:05:00.958
The Cabbie's Code!
It's an oath of confidentiality we take.

00:05:01.042 --> 00:05:04.542
You know, like your doctors,
your priests, your medieval knights.

00:05:04.625 --> 00:05:06.708
You do understand, don't you, love?

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:08.417
Of course.

00:05:09.625 --> 00:05:12.917
Let me tell you about my code.

00:05:12.958 --> 00:05:17.000
When somebody doesn't give me
what I want, I remove their body parts.

00:05:17.083 --> 00:05:19.125
I start with the nasal hair.

00:05:19.208 --> 00:05:20.375
Ow.

00:05:20.458 --> 00:05:22.417
And then I move on to something juicy.

00:05:23.208 --> 00:05:26.208
That's my code and I always stick to it.

00:05:27.125 --> 00:05:29.000
Do you always stick to yours?

00:05:29.167 --> 00:05:31.333
- Well, it's not even really a code.
- No?

00:05:31.417 --> 00:05:34.875
It's more a set of guidelines
than a binding ethos.

00:05:34.917 --> 00:05:38.167
Then tell me,
where did you take the bear?

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:41.042
- Windsor Gardens!
- Thank you.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:45.458
I wouldn't go up the Westway this
time of night. You wanna go north...

00:05:47.833 --> 00:05:50.417
- Bye, Paddington.
- Goodbye, Jonathan.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:52.875
- Good luck.
- Bye, Paddington.

00:05:54.667 --> 00:05:57.625
Bye.
I hope you all have a good day.

00:05:59.583 --> 00:06:03.458
I really do like these French
sandwiches, Mrs Bird. Very exotic.

00:06:03.583 --> 00:06:06.417
- Can I help you, son?
- Just a sec.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:09.292
You've been in there for 47 minutes.
Either a very long call

00:06:09.375 --> 00:06:12.875
or you're placing unauthorised
advertising in a public phone box.

00:06:12.958 --> 00:06:14.417
I'm terribly sorry.

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:17.542
♪ Hello

00:06:17.625 --> 00:06:22.417
♪ Is it me you're looking for?
I can see...

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.625
No problem... madam.

00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:28.000
Many apologies if I disturbed you.
It's just,

00:06:28.083 --> 00:06:30.833
I keep an eye on all
the comings and goings and...

00:06:30.917 --> 00:06:33.375
there's been a few unsavoury
characters hanging around.

00:06:33.958 --> 00:06:36.333
Let's get this
over and done with.

00:06:36.417 --> 00:06:39.667
There's even been a bear.
A most unpleasant creature.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:44.292
As a matter of fact,
that bear is the reason I'm here.

00:06:56.708 --> 00:06:59.625
Welcome to the
Geographers' Guild. Are you members?

00:06:59.708 --> 00:07:01.500
No, but we are looking for one.

00:07:01.625 --> 00:07:05.083
- The name?
- We don't actually know the name,

00:07:05.167 --> 00:07:08.958
but we do know he went on an expedition
you funded to Darkest Peru.

00:07:09.042 --> 00:07:10.333
Darkest Peru.

